n></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">A</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Mat.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.ger\">ger</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">x</span> <span class=\"fn\">y</span> <span class=\"fn\">A</span>)</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Mat.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.data\">data</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a>   <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Mat.html#BLAS.Float64.mapMat\">mapMat</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">A</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Mat.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.data\">data</a></span> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">A</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Mat.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.off\">off</a></span> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">A</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Mat.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.ld\">ld</a></span> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">0</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">fun (<span class=\"fn\">i</span> <span class=\"fn\">j</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>) (<span class=\"fn\">v</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>) =&gt; <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#ite\">if</a> (<span class=\"fn\">α</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#BEq.beq\">==</a> <span class=\"fn\">0</span>) <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#ite\">then</a> <span class=\"fn\">v</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#ite\">else</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.gerAt\">gerAt</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">x</span> <span class=\"fn\">y</span> <span class=\"fn\">i</span> <span class=\"fn\">j</span> <span class=\"fn\">v</span></span></span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The array of `ger α x y A` is the array of `A` with its elements updated.","docLink":"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.data_ger","kind":"theorem","line":705,"name":"BLAS.Float64.Mat.data_ger","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-blas/blob/0b5b806802a404d62a8c76bf36594f35690cd2ba/BLAS/Float64/Level2.lean#L705-L712"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.ger\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float64</span>.<span class=\"name\">Mat</span>.<span class=\"name\">ger</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Vec.html#BLAS.Float64.Vec\">Vec</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Vec.html#BLAS.Float64.Vec\">Vec</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">A</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Mat.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Mat.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`ger α x y A` is `α * x * yᵀ + A`, by the loops of the reference BLAS: for each column `j`, it\nadds `x` times `α * y[j]`. As in the reference BLAS, it returns `A` when `α = 0`, and skips the\ncolumns with `y[j] = 0`, without reading `x`, so an infinity or a `NaN` in `x` doesn't reach\nthem. It updates `A` in place when its array is not shared, and leaves the elements of the array\noutside `A` unchanged.","docLink":"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.ger","kind":"def","line":689,"name":"BLAS.Float64.Mat.ger","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-blas/blob/0b5b806802a404d62a8c76bf36594f35690cd2ba/BLAS/Float64/Level2.lean#L689-L703"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.gerData_eq\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float64</span>.<span class=\"name\">Mat</span>.<span class=\"name\">gerData_eq</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Vec.html#BLAS.Float64.Vec\">Vec</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Vec.html#BLAS.Float64.Vec\">Vec</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">A</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Mat.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_t