lass=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">y</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Vec.html#BLAS.Float64.Vec.data\">data</a></span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Float64/Stride.html#ScalarArray.Float64Array.modifyAt\">modifyAt</a></span> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">y</span>.<a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Vec.html#BLAS.Float64.Vec.stride\">stride</a></span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Stride.html#ScalarArray.Stride.idx\">idx</a></span> <span class=\"fn\">0</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.gemvTAt\">gemvTAt</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span> <span class=\"fn\">A</span> <span class=\"fn\">x</span> <span class=\"fn\">β</span>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The array of `gemvT α A x β y` is the array of `y` with its elements updated.","docLink":"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.data_gemvT","kind":"theorem","line":561,"name":"BLAS.Float64.Mat.data_gemvT","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-blas/blob/0b5b806802a404d62a8c76bf36594f35690cd2ba/BLAS/Float64/Level2.lean#L561-L574"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.gemvT\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float64</span>.<span class=\"name\">Mat</span>.<span class=\"name\">gemvT</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">A</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Mat.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat\">Mat</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Vec.html#BLAS.Float64.Vec\">Vec</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Vec.html#BLAS.Float64.Vec\">Vec</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Vec.html#BLAS.Float64.Vec\">Vec</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`gemvT α A x β y` is `α * Aᵀ * x + β * y`, with the operations of the reference BLAS, in its order\nfor each element: for each `j`, it sums the products `A[i, j] * x[i]` of column `j` of `A` and `x`\nfrom the left, and adds `α` times the sum to `β * y[j]`. It computes the sums of four columns in\neach pass over `x`, which gives the same sums and lets their additions overlap. As in the reference\nBLAS, it returns `y` when `m = 0`, sets `y[j]` to `0` without reading it before adding the sum when\n`β = 0`, and only scales `y` when `α = 0`, without reading `A` or `x`. It updates `y` in place when\nits array is not shared, and leaves the elements of the array outside `y` unchanged.","docLink":"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.gemvT","kind":"def","line":536,"name":"BLAS.Float64.Mat.gemvT","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-blas/blob/0b5b806802a404d62a8c76bf36594f35690cd2ba/BLAS/Float64/Level2.lean#L536-L559"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./BLAS/Float64/Level2.html#BLAS.Float64.Mat.gemvTData_eq\"><span class=\"name\">BLAS</span>.<span class=\"name\">Float64</span>.<span class=